================================================================================
CHANGES FROM UPSTREAM
================================================================================

Patchfly is a derivative work of Shorebird with the following
categories of change:

1. Rebrand
   - Project name "Shorebird" → "Patchfly" across CLI, SDK, server,
     docs site, and all user-facing strings.
   - Command-line binary "shorebird" → "patchfly".
   - Default CDN endpoint, SDK key format, package name, etc.

2. Distribution
   - Default install path no longer assumes a vendor-managed CDN;
     install scripts point at https://cdn.patchfly.dev by default.
   - One-line installer scripts ship in a dedicated public repo
     (fatmuh/patchfly-install).

3. Server
   - Hardened `_downloadUrl()` helper to avoid the well-known
     "localhost:8080" bug that leaked into production responses
     (server commit e647b2b). All six download endpoints now route
     through a single resolver that consults the active storage
     backend and falls back to environment-driven defaults.
   - `PULTFLUT_*` environment variables retained as a fallback for
     the rebrand period; new `PATCHFLY_*` variables are canonical.

4. CLI
   - `patches promote` introduced as the canonical patch-management
     command, with `promote` retained as a deprecation alias.
   - Build-time version injection via Dart's `String.fromEnvironment`
     with `--dart-define=VERSION=...` so the compiled binary reports
     the exact version that was released.
   - 13 commands total, each with a full --help, error hints, and
     non-interactive flags suited for CI.

5. SDK
   - Public sample (fatmuh/patchfly-sample) ships with the SDK
     stubbed behind the same Dart API; a one-import swap
     (`import 'package:patchfly/patchfly.dart';`) is the only
     change required to go from stub to real.

6. Native engine
   - Rust updater (fatmuh/patchfly-updater) builds against
     `bsdiff`/`bzip2` for the patch delta. ABI filters, ProGuard
     rules, and NDK version pinned in CI.

7. Documentation
   - Hosted at https://docs.patchfly.dev (separate from the
     product site at https://patchfly.dev). The docs site
     (fatmuh/patchfly-web) is itself a Next.js 16 + Fumadocs 16
     project, force-pushed on rebuild; the previous Astro 5
     docs are not preserved.
   - All self-hosting content removed as part of the
     repositioning to managed-cloud-only.

